cates that anger reactions are within a minimal to mild","bbox":[91.0394,187.49301,559.33142,198.49301],"origin":[91.0394,195.99249],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"range as compared to individuals who have experienced trauma but are managing their","bbox":[91.0394,199.59299,515.95837,210.59299],"origin":[91.0394,208.09247],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"emotional responses effectively. This suggests that anger is likely not currently a significant","bbox":[91.0394,211.69296,534.27344,222.69296],"origin":[91.0394,220.19244],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"barrier to recovery or causing substantial difficulties in daily life.","bbox":[91.0394,223.79294,398.53333,234.79294],"origin":[91.0394,232.29242],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Scoring and Interpretation Information","bbox":[34.3464,255.61357,290.26636,269.61359],"origin":[34.3464,266.43109],"font":"Helvetica-Bold","size":14.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"For comprehensive information on the DAR-5, ","bbox":[91.0393,274.86966,318.45328,285.86966],"origin":[91.0393,283.36914],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"see here","bbox":[318.45401,274.86954,361.255,285.86954],"origin":[318.45401,283.36902],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#0000ff","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":".","bbox":[361.254,274.86954,364.31201,285.86954],"origin":[361.254,283.36902],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"The DAR-5 produces a total score ranging from 5 to 25. Higher scores indicate greater levels of","bbox":[91.039,299.06955,555.06305,310.06955],"origin":[91.039,307.56903],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"problematic anger.","bbox":[91.039,311.16953,182.12997,322.16953],"origin":[91.039,319.66901],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Score interpretation is guided by an established empirical cut-off (12+), in addition to percentile","bbox":[91.039,335.36954,551.71912,346.36954],"origin":[91.039,343.86902],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"rankings within serving personnel and clinical PTSD samples for comparison.","bbox":[91.039,347.46915,466.38092,358.46915],"origin":[91.039,355.96863],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Upon the first administration of the DAR-5, a bar graph displaying the total raw score is","bbox":[91.039,371.66956,512.87793,382.66956],"origin":[91.039,380.16904],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"presented with serving personnel percentile labels on the right-hand side. A second graph is","bbox":[91.039,383.76956,538.58502,394.76956],"origin":[91.039,392.26904],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"shown displaying the client's score relative to serving personnel as well as those with PTSD.","bbox":[91.039,395.86957,539.42096,406.86957],"origin":[91.039,404.36905],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"This helps interpret whether a client’s anger reactions are within the range typically observed in","bbox":[91.039,407.96957,553.22607,418.96957],"origin":[91.039,416.46906],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"serving personnel, or whether they reflect the more severe and persistent anger characteristic of","bbox":[91.039,420.06958,558.737,431.06958],"origin":[91.039,428.56906],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"clinical PTSD. When the assessment is administered multiple times, a longitudinal line graph is","bbox":[91.039,432.16959,551.97205,443.16959],"origin":[91.039,440.66907],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"generated to track changes in the total raw score over time.","bbox":[91.039,444.26959,380.22897,455.26959],"origin":[91.039,452.76907],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"When tracking DAR-5 score changes across administrations, clinicians can evaluate treatment","bbox":[91.039,468.4696,550.146,479.4696],"origin":[91.039,476.96909],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"response and the effectiveness of anger-focused interventions. A shift of approximately 2 points","bbox":[91.039,480.56961,556.32806,491.56961],"origin":[91.039,489.06909],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"or more suggests meaningful improvement, following minimally important difference guidelines","bbox":[91.039,492.66962,550.13507,503.66962],"origin":[91.039,501.1691],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"(Turner et al., 2010). This corresponds to approximately half a standard deviation. The scale has","bbox":[91.039,504.76962,559.96912,515.76965],"origin":[91.039,513.2691],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"demonstrated sensitivity to change following PTSD treatment, with reductions in anger scores","bbox":[91.039,516.86969,545.88904,527.86969],"origin":[91.039,525.36914],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"observed alongside improvements in PTSD symptoms.","bbox":[91.039,528.96967,358.78998,539.96967],"origin":[91.039,537.46912],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Interpretation at the item level may also be clinically useful. Examining patterns across these","bbox":[91.039,553.16968,540.38898,564.16968],"origin":[91.039,561.66913],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"dimensions can inform treatment planning. For example, high frequency scores with relatively","bbox":[91.039,565.26971,545.26202,576.26971],"origin":[91.039,573.76917],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"low intensity and aggression ratings may suggest chronic irritability rather than explosive anger.","bbox":[91.039,577.36969,555.05206,588.36969],"origin":[91.039,585.86914],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Additionally, elevated duration scores relative to other items may suggest difficulties with","bbox":[91.039,589.46967,520.82001,600.46967],"origin":[91.039,597.96912],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"rumination or emotion regulation that could benefit from cognitive restructuring interventions.","bbox":[91.039,601.5697,539.784,612.5697],"origin":[91.039,610.06915],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Client Responses","bbox":[34.346,649.36182,151.82001,663.36182],"origin":[34.346,660.17932],"font":"Helvetica-Bold","size":14.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"None or","bbox":[273.01501,668.51111,302.41589,676.77673],"origin":[273.01501,674.89777],"font":"Helvetica","size":8.265629768371582,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"almost none","bbox":[265.20407,677.60327,310.22705,685.8689],"origin":[265.20407,683.98993],"font":"Helvetica","size":8.265629768371582,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"of the time","bbox":[268.41931,686.6955,307.01163,694.96112],"origin":[268.41931,693.08215],"font":"Helvetica","size":8.265629768371582,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"A little of the","bbox":[323.85522,672.82996,370.6308,681.32996],"origin":[323.85522,679.39771],"font":"Helvetica","size":8.5,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"time","bbox":[339.21503,682.17993,355.271